# .clang-format -- one style for the whole project (source + tests + headers).
#
# The project brief accepts the clang-format defaults; this file pins them so a
# bare `clang-format -i` gives the same result on every machine (without a
# config file the outcome depends on the local ~/.clang-format and version).
#
# Deviations from the pure LLVM default, and why:
#   * ColumnLimit 100        -- the default 80 re-wraps 700+ already readable
#                               lines (template parameter lists, CUDA launch
#                               configs); 100 keeps the diff small without
#                               hiding logic.
#   * ReflowComments: false  -- the hand-laid-out comment blocks and the ASCII
#                               separators survive untouched.
#   * SortIncludes: false    -- the relative includes (common.cuh, types.cuh)
#                               are ordered by dependency, not alphabetically.
#   * AlignConsecutiveMacros -- keeps the cuda->musa alias table in
#                               backend.cuh readable (the LLVM default would
#                               flatten it).
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
Standard: c++17
ColumnLimit: 100
ReflowComments: false
SortIncludes: false
AlignConsecutiveMacros: AcrossEmptyLinesAndComments
...
